.SS deq render
Render shapes to files.
.PP
\fBdeq render\fR <shape...> [options]
.TP
\fI<shape...>\fR
Shape ids (see deq list).
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR
Output format. Default svg. Values: svg, svg-layered, svg-sprite, html, jsx, tsx, vue, svelte, data-uri, css-background, css-mask, pdf, ai, eps, png, jpg, webp, avif, ico, favicon, psd, figma, spec-json.
.TP
\fB\-\-size\fR \fIpx\fR
Width and height in px, 1 to 8192. Default 24.
.TP
\fB\-\-layered\fR
SVG with one Inkscape layer per shape layer (same as --format svg-layered).
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fIpath\fR
Output file, or a directory for several files; - writes one file to stdout. Default: the current directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIcolor\fR
Stroke and dot colour (any CSS colour). Default currentColor.
.TP
\fB\-\-stroke\-width\fR \fIn\fR
Stroke width in grid units, 0.05 to 12. Default 2.
.TP
\fB\-\-absolute\-stroke\-width\fR
Keep the stroke the same width in px at any size.
.TP
\fB\-\-fill\fR \fIcolor\fR
Fill for closed outlines, or none. Default none.
.TP
\fB\-\-fill\-opacity\fR \fI0-1\fR
Opacity of the fill. Default 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-stroke\-opacity\fR \fI0-1\fR
Opacity of strokes and dots. Default 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-linecap\fR \fIlinecap\fR
Line ends. Default round. Values: round, butt, square.
.TP
\fB\-\-linejoin\fR \fIlinejoin\fR
Line corners. Default round. Values: round, miter, bevel.
.TP
\fB\-\-dot\-scale\fR \fIn\fR
Multiply every dot radius, 0.1 to 4. Default 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-rotation\fR \fIdeg\fR
Rotate clockwise about the centre. Default 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-flip\-x\fR
Mirror left to right.
.TP
\fB\-\-flip\-y\fR
Mirror top to bottom.
.TP
\fB\-\-padding\fR \fIn\fR
Space around the 24 x 24 canvas in grid units, 0 to 24. Default 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-background\fR \fIcolor\fR
Background colour, or none. Default none.
.TP
\fB\-\-layer\-color\fR \fIlayer=color\fR
Colour of one layer, for example sun=#FEBD11 (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fItext\fR
Accessible title. Default the English name; "" marks the image decorative.
.TP
\fB\-\-param\fR \fIname=value\fR
Shape parameter, for example rays=9 (repeatable; see deq info).
.TP
\fB\-\-current\-color\fR \fIcolor\fR
What currentColor means in PDF and image formats. Default black.
.TP
\fB\-\-matte\fR \fIcolor\fR
